A USER can hold one or many ROLEs; each ROLE can be held by one or many USERs, except the Super Admin ROLE and the Level 3 Reviewer ROLE, each of which can be held by at most one USER at a time.
A Document Source, Level 1 Reviewer, or Level 2 Reviewer can submit one or many DOCUMENTs; each DOCUMENT is submitted by exactly one Document Source, Level 1 Reviewer, or Level 2 Reviewer.
A DOCUMENT can have zero or many REVISIONs; each REVISION belongs to exactly one DOCUMENT.
A returned DOCUMENT can be resubmitted only by the USER who originally submitted it; each REVISION of a returned DOCUMENT is submitted by that same USER.
A DOCUMENT is classified under exactly one DOCUMENT TYPE; a DOCUMENT TYPE can classify one or many DOCUMENTs.
A Level 1 Reviewer, Level 2 Reviewer, or Level 3 Reviewer can be assigned as the current reviewer of zero or many DOCUMENTs; each DOCUMENT that is currently under review is assigned to exactly one Level 1 Reviewer, Level 2 Reviewer, or Level 3 Reviewer as its current reviewer.
A USER who submitted a DOCUMENT, whether as a Document Source, Level 1 Reviewer, or Level 2 Reviewer, cannot be assigned as the current reviewer of that DOCUMENT or perform a REVIEW on it, even if the same USER also holds a reviewer ROLE (Self-Review Restriction).
A resubmitted DOCUMENT must be assigned to the same Level 1 Reviewer previously assigned to it; a different eligible Level 1 Reviewer may be assigned only if the previous Level 1 Reviewer is no longer active or eligible.
A Level 1 Reviewer or Level 2 Reviewer can have zero or many REVIEWER ELIGIBILITY records; each REVIEWER ELIGIBILITY record belongs to exactly one Level 1 Reviewer or Level 2 Reviewer.
An original DOCUMENT submission and each of its REVISIONs can have zero or many REVIEWs; each REVIEW evaluates exactly one DOCUMENT submission, either the original submission or one REVISION.
A Level 1 Reviewer, Level 2 Reviewer, or Level 3 Reviewer can perform zero or many REVIEWs; each REVIEW is performed by exactly one Level 1 Reviewer, Level 2 Reviewer, or Level 3 Reviewer.
A DOCUMENT can trigger zero or many NOTIFICATIONs; each NOTIFICATION is triggered by zero or one DOCUMENT.
A Document Source, Level 1 Reviewer, Level 2 Reviewer, or Level 3 Reviewer can receive zero or many NOTIFICATIONs; each NOTIFICATION is received by exactly one Document Source, Level 1 Reviewer, Level 2 Reviewer, or Level 3 Reviewer.
Any USER can generate zero or many AUDIT LOG entries; each AUDIT LOG entry is generated by exactly one USER.
A DOCUMENT can have zero or many AUDIT LOG entries; each AUDIT LOG entry is associated with zero or one DOCUMENT.
